  "id": "excise-glom_matching.py-glom.matching._precedence",
  "instruction": "Implement key precedence calculation in `glom.matching._precedence` for dictionary pattern matching specs.\n\nWhen matching dictionary keys against spec patterns, a given target key may match multiple candidate spec keys (such as an exact literal value, a type specifier, or a predicate matcher). To ensure deterministic and expected matching order, `_precedence` must return an ordering value (where lower values are tried earlier and higher values are tried later) according to the specificity of the spec key:\n\n1. Exact literal values (such as strings, numbers, booleans, and other non-spec objects) must take highest priority / lowest precedence rank.\n2. Spec types and pattern matchers (such as types/classes, `Match`, `Check`, `Regex`, and boolean matchers like `And`, `Or`, `Not`, or wrapped matchers) must be ordered appropriately so that more specific constraints are attempted before broader or catch-all matchers.\n3. Wrapped and nested matchers must correctly compute precedence based on their inner/underlying matchers or structure.\n\nAll existing `glom.matching` tests, including nested structure matching, sample cases, and wrapped matchers, must pass.",
